Jorge Llamb=EDas wrote:
> You don't need to worry about any of this in order to use the
> language, but surely there is no harm in people discussing these
> things?

If they are talking is Lojban, probably not.  If they are talking in=20
English, especially with you involved, some will see the discussion as=20
"xorlo mod 2" and then people will be asking Robin on IRC "Are you using=20
xorlo mod 2 or xorlo mod 1?".

That was why, ages back, I had no trouble with And Rosta setting up=20
jboske as a list for such discussions as people talking about how Lojban=20
could be more logical than it is, and about improvements appropriate for=20
LoCCan3.

Experimental cmavo are kinda the border ground between the two.  It=20
doesn't necessarily harm the existing language to propose a new cmavo,=20
put THAT is where the "let usage decide" is supposed to come in.  If=20
people are unwilling to start using an experimental cmavo without it=20
being prescribed, it probably isn't necessary, or at least not=20
appreciated.  And it likely won't be appreciated with people seeing it=20
in use and contrasted with the language without.  Even then, the people=20
  who need to see it as an "improvement" will be those who actually use=20
the language, which is why discussing it in Lojban is a strong plus.

lojbab

